From 1d5cd5b7459e14af9a319c594da4066476cbc677 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Solomon Kinard <solomonkinard@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:39:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/32] Extensions: WAR: Require explicit declaration for
 generated paths

ExtensionURLLoader serves synthetic endpoints not backed by files on
disk, such as _favicon and _generated_background_page.html. Because
web_accessible_resources is matched by URLPattern, a blanket wildcard
like "*" unintentionally exposed these paths to external web origins,
which could allow arbitrary web origins to probe profile favicon data.

Exclude generated paths from blanket wildcards in
WebAccessibleResourcesInfo::IsResourceWebAccessible, requiring
extensions to explicitly declare them (e.g. "_favicon/*") to make
them accessible to matching web origins. This supports the
documented pattern for fetching favicons in content scripts while
preventing accidental exposure via wildcards.

Ensure _generated_background_page.html is never considered web
accessible, and restrict it to the extension's own origin in
ExtensionURLLoader.

The new behavior is gated behind the
kRestrictGeneratedPathsInWebAccessibleResources feature flag, which
is disabled by default. A follow-up CL enables it.

Add unit tests in WebAccessibleResourcesManifestTest and
ExtensionProtocolsTest, and browser tests in FaviconApiTest for web
origins, explicit allowlisting, and content script execution, with
the feature flag both enabled and disabled.

Fixed: 506142100
